angle-metal-fixes.patch — generic fixes for the ANGLE Metal backend
====================================================================
(developed in the Vice City port for visionOS; not game-specific)

Base:        ANGLE e4499e6b2835a6996507f1b99920bc56f0122573
Order:       apply klepton.patch first, then this patch (git apply).
Created:     2026-09-23 from the working tree (tag vc-local-state-20260923
             in the angle-src checkout holds the complete state).

Contents (four groups):

1. Deferred GC (fix for the rain + foveation flicker, PRODUCTION):
   mtl_buffer_manager.{h,mm}, ContextMtl.{h,mm} —
   the BufferManager's memory-based GC no longer flushes in the middle of a
   pass that has a rate map (pass restart + store/load under a rate map =
   flicker); it is deferred and run at the frame boundary (ContextMtl::flush
   -> runPendingGC). Cap KL_MTL_GC_DEFER_CAP_MB (default 256), off switch
   KL_MTL_GC_DEFER=0, floor override KL_MTL_BUFFER_GC_MB.

2. Non-triangle skip under a rate map (PRODUCTION):
   mtl_command_buffer.{h,mm} — Metal only allows triangles under a
   rasterization rate map; the draw* methods skip lines/points instead of
   aborting. (Previously only mentioned in angle-build.md, never saved.)

3. Diagnostic probes (active only with KL_ANGLE_VRR_TRACE=1, banner rev=10):
   mtl_common.mm (banner), mtl_state_cache.mm (convertToMetalDesc trace),
   ContextMtl.mm (endEncoding/flushCB trace with dladdr),
   mtl_command_buffer.mm (encode/s replay timing, cmds/s command count,
   mNumDraws), mtl_buffer_manager.mm (bufferGC trace).

4. Werror pragmas (needed from the Xcode 27 toolchain on):
   a file-local "#pragma clang diagnostic ignored
   -Wunsafe-buffer-usage[-in-libc-call]" in all six probe files — Chromium's
   unsafe-buffers lint otherwise turns fprintf into an error. Deliberately
   NOT global (treat_warnings_as_errors stays on), see BUILD.md section 7.

Note: the implicit MSAA path of the guest (VC_MSAA_IMPLICIT) depends on
groups 1+2. Klepton's physicalPassthrough (rate-map-aware blit) lives in
klepton.patch, NOT here — and is still missing in unresolveIfNeeded (known
gap; consequence for guests: never start a pass on a memoryless MSAA
attachment with loadAction=Load under a rate map, see README).

